   "l": "Therefore, abidingly without desire, thereby to behold its subtlety;",
   "i": "So: constantly free of desire, and you behold what is subtle in it;",
   "n": "以 is the workhorse preposition 'by means of' with its object left out — 'by that means', hence 'so as to'. The same crux as above reaches this line: read 常無，欲以觀其妙 and it becomes 'constantly non-being — desire thereby to behold its subtlety.' We follow Wang Bi.",
