   "l": "These two — together they come forth yet differ in name; alike, call them the dark.\nDark, and dark once more —\nthe gate of the many subtleties.",
   "i": "The two come out together but go by different names; both alike may be called the dark. Dark, and dark again — the gateway of every wonder.",
   "n": "謂之玄: here 之 is the object pronoun, 'call them dark' — the same character that was 'of' three lines ago. One character, two jobs, no ending to tell them apart; only position does. 玄 is not evil-dark: it is the blue-black of deep water, of something too far down to make out. 玄 and 門 are traditionally taken as rhyming in Old Chinese; in Mandarin (xuán / mén) the rhyme is gone.",
